WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.656 --> 00:00:02.689
- Anybody want to jump in with me?

00:00:02.689 --> 00:00:03.599
Hell no you don't.

00:00:03.599 --> 00:00:05.470
Sounds like the stupidest idea ever.

00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:07.149
You know people always
ask me, how do you do this

00:00:07.149 --> 00:00:08.572
and you have to do it.

00:00:08.572 --> 00:00:10.873
We believed in the sport and the athletes.

00:00:10.873 --> 00:00:13.152
And we believed that this
could be a global franchise.

00:00:13.152 --> 00:00:14.988
You know what happens when
you get $37 million dollars

00:00:14.988 --> 00:00:17.163
and you're a fighter...

00:00:17.163 --> 00:00:18.378
(audience laugher)

00:00:18.378 --> 00:00:19.738
I don't want to get punched in the face.

00:00:19.738 --> 00:00:22.081
Imagine if they did this,
and imagine if they did that.

00:00:22.081 --> 00:00:23.163
This thing could be big.

00:00:23.163 --> 00:00:25.053
Fighting is the first sport ever

00:00:25.053 --> 00:00:26.763
and it will be the last sport ever.

00:00:26.763 --> 00:00:28.381
It will be around till the day we die.

00:00:28.381 --> 00:00:29.776
If you don't think the UFC is exciting,

00:00:29.776 --> 00:00:31.071
you got to be a lunatic.

00:00:31.071 --> 00:00:32.618
Okay, I don't know what
you, you want to see people

00:00:32.618 --> 00:00:34.095
get beat with baseball bats?

00:00:34.095 --> 00:00:38.524
Anything that you do in life,
when you become successful,

00:00:38.524 --> 00:00:40.043
it has to do with timing.

00:00:40.043 --> 00:00:43.630
I already know and have
my mind set, and you know,

00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:45.182
I know that this is what my life's

00:00:45.182 --> 00:00:46.378
going to be like for the next two years.

00:00:46.378 --> 00:00:49.520
Any of you guys ever watch my video blogs?

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:50.470
Two people, great.

00:00:50.470 --> 00:00:51.872
(audience laughs)

00:00:51.872 --> 00:00:54.570
- He's an American
businessman and entrepreneur.

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:56.398
- He's the President of
the Mixed Martial Arts

00:00:56.398 --> 00:01:00.207
organization Ultimate
Fighting Championship or UFC.

00:01:00.207 --> 00:01:04.374
- In 2014, his estimated
net worth was $350 million.

00:01:05.499 --> 00:01:09.666
- He's Dana White and here are
his top 10 rules for success.

00:01:12.026 --> 00:01:13.740
- If you look back six years ago,

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.133
money was growing on trees.

00:01:15.133 --> 00:01:16.743
Anybody could get a loan,
you could pick up the phone

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:18.785
and anybody could get a loan for anything.

00:01:18.785 --> 00:01:22.110
Business, house, cars, it
was easy to raise money.

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:25.156
So, you know we go out there,
we make this thing work.

00:01:25.156 --> 00:01:26.987
The first season of the
Ultimate Fighter happens.

00:01:26.987 --> 00:01:29.203
This thing skyrockets, starts to take off.

00:01:29.203 --> 00:01:32.082
So of course, the fight business
is a fun business to be in.

00:01:32.082 --> 00:01:34.497
So everybody starts
diving into this thing.

00:01:34.497 --> 00:01:36.927
Well it's easy, right, you
just throw 3 letters together

00:01:36.927 --> 00:01:39.677
and buy a cage and put on fights.

00:01:39.677 --> 00:01:40.540
Anybody could do that.

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:42.537
So these guys go out and
the biggest mistake that

00:01:42.537 --> 00:01:45.766
everybody makes when they
try to compete with us,

00:01:45.766 --> 00:01:47.614
is they try to compete with us.

00:01:47.614 --> 00:01:50.988
First of all, we didn't
come out yesterday and put

00:01:50.988 --> 00:01:53.309
together an organization
and now we're on FOX and

00:01:53.309 --> 00:01:54.974
now we're on pay-per-view.

00:01:54.974 --> 00:01:59.688
Anything you do, nothing
happens over night man,

00:01:59.688 --> 00:02:03.204
it seems that way but it's all hard work.

00:02:03.204 --> 00:02:06.204
I have been on planes,
trains and automobiles

00:02:06.204 --> 00:02:08.967
for the last 13 years
out selling this sport,

00:02:08.967 --> 00:02:12.746
getting deals done, getting
doors slammed in my face,

00:02:12.746 --> 00:02:15.950
you name it, it's all happened.

00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:17.845
These guys come out and they
just start throwing money

00:02:17.845 --> 00:02:20.724
around and start trying to be the UFC.

00:02:20.724 --> 00:02:22.012
Don't try to be the UFC.

00:02:22.012 --> 00:02:23.725
The first thing you have to do when you

00:02:23.725 --> 00:02:26.413
start a business is
know exactly who you are

00:02:26.413 --> 00:02:28.141
and what is your game plan.

00:02:28.141 --> 00:02:30.157
You know, what are we going to do?

00:02:30.157 --> 00:02:32.558
First year is where you're looking.

00:02:32.558 --> 00:02:34.108
What are we going to do first year?

00:02:34.108 --> 00:02:36.366
You make it through that first
year and you're still alive,

00:02:36.366 --> 00:02:38.732
alright, what's our three year plan.

00:02:38.732 --> 00:02:40.622
You get into your three
year plan, and that's how

00:02:40.622 --> 00:02:42.232
you start to build your company.

00:02:42.232 --> 00:02:43.582
The last thing on earth...

00:02:43.582 --> 00:02:46.527
This is how stupid it is,
okay, be like we're all

00:02:46.527 --> 00:02:48.089
sitting around, this is my living room.

00:02:48.089 --> 00:02:50.041
We're all here, we're hanging
out in my living room,

00:02:50.041 --> 00:02:52.284
and we're watching NASCAR.

00:02:52.284 --> 00:02:54.911
Okay, holy (bleep)!

00:02:54.911 --> 00:02:57.996
Look at all the people at NASCAR!

00:02:57.996 --> 00:03:00.158
These guys must be making tons of money.

00:03:00.158 --> 00:03:01.517
You know what we should do?

00:03:01.517 --> 00:03:03.197
We should go get a
couple of their drivers,

00:03:03.197 --> 00:03:05.258
and lets start our own race league.

00:03:05.258 --> 00:03:07.525
And we'll compete with NASCAR.

00:03:07.525 --> 00:03:09.562
Anybody want to jump in with me?

00:03:09.562 --> 00:03:10.503
Hell no you don't!

00:03:10.503 --> 00:03:12.566
Sounds like the stupidest idea ever!

00:03:12.566 --> 00:03:14.652
But people think they
can do it with the UFC.

00:03:14.652 --> 00:03:17.235
UFC's been around for 20 years.

00:03:18.362 --> 00:03:22.237
Twenty years and this November
it'll be 13 years for us.

00:03:22.237 --> 00:03:23.724
And you think you're going
to just dive right in

00:03:23.724 --> 00:03:25.063
and start throwing money around?

00:03:25.063 --> 00:03:27.284
You will go out of business so fast.

00:03:27.284 --> 00:03:28.942
You know people always ask
me, how do you do this?

00:03:28.942 --> 00:03:30.282
And you have to do it.

00:03:30.282 --> 00:03:34.105
I mean, when you're building
a business like the UFC

00:03:34.105 --> 00:03:37.110
or any other business, you
know you have to work and

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:38.864
it never gets easier.

00:03:38.864 --> 00:03:42.535
It's funny, because 13 years
now, and we're in 175 countries

00:03:42.535 --> 00:03:45.244
and 23 different languages,
and over a billion homes

00:03:45.244 --> 00:03:47.114
worldwide on television.

00:03:47.114 --> 00:03:49.781
And you think, when you're
early on building, it's like

00:03:49.781 --> 00:03:52.180
when we get to this point
you know I can probably

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:53.166
- Chill out.

00:03:53.166 --> 00:03:56.162
- Right, exactly. And it
just gets harder and harder.

00:03:56.162 --> 00:03:57.853
It doesn't get easier, it gets worse.

00:03:57.853 --> 00:03:58.969
Take money out of the equation,

00:03:58.969 --> 00:04:00.903
him and his brother are billionaires,

00:04:00.903 --> 00:04:02.555
two of the hardest working
guys that I've ever met.

00:04:02.555 --> 00:04:04.516
- Middle class billionaires.

00:04:04.516 --> 00:04:07.927
- We got into this thing
because we're very passionate

00:04:07.927 --> 00:04:09.020
about the sport.

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:11.050
We didn't get into it,
believe me, when we got into

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:15.217
this sport, these guys...their
peers were laughing at them.

00:04:16.424 --> 00:04:17.258
- That's true.

00:04:17.258 --> 00:04:19.508
- Said this was the stupidest
investment they'd ever made,

00:04:19.508 --> 00:04:24.037
they're losing tons of money,
the UFC was a joke, and

00:04:24.037 --> 00:04:26.803
believe me, we've went
through a lot of ridicule and

00:04:26.803 --> 00:04:28.719
everything else when we
first bought this thing,

00:04:28.719 --> 00:04:30.341
and now that its turned
around, everybody thinks its

00:04:30.341 --> 00:04:31.617
the greatest thing in
the world and they wish

00:04:31.617 --> 00:04:32.589
they were apart of it.

00:04:32.589 --> 00:04:34.469
We didn't buy this because
we thought that it was going

00:04:34.469 --> 00:04:35.909
to be, you know, oh we were going

00:04:35.909 --> 00:04:37.859
to make billions of dollars.

00:04:37.859 --> 00:04:40.376
We believed in the sport and the athletes,

00:04:40.376 --> 00:04:43.027
and we believed that this
could be a global franchise,

00:04:43.027 --> 00:04:44.864
that this thing could be built into

00:04:44.864 --> 00:04:46.529
what we're building it into now,

00:04:46.529 --> 00:04:50.468
and everyday when we get up,
we know what the prize is,

00:04:50.468 --> 00:04:51.301
we know what the goal is,

00:04:51.301 --> 00:04:54.176
we want the UFC, we're
going to put on an event

00:04:54.176 --> 00:04:57.097
everywhere in every city in every country,

00:04:57.097 --> 00:04:59.289
all over this planet,
and make this the biggest

00:04:59.289 --> 00:05:00.122
sport in the world.

00:05:00.122 --> 00:05:01.469
- You want to be bigger than the NFL?

00:05:01.469 --> 00:05:02.491
That's going to be hard.

00:05:02.491 --> 00:05:05.039
- The thing that we do
different than any other sport,

00:05:05.039 --> 00:05:07.503
especially boxing, when you
think about boxing, right,

00:05:07.503 --> 00:05:08.942
they do the same thing.

00:05:08.942 --> 00:05:11.206
And how many guys in
here, who's boxing fans?

00:05:11.206 --> 00:05:14.252
I am, I'll raise my hand too, okay?

00:05:14.252 --> 00:05:16.252
Like five of ya, and me.

00:05:17.176 --> 00:05:19.650
But here's the thing
that boxing did, and the

00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:22.676
question was asked earlier
on the decline of boxing,

00:05:22.676 --> 00:05:26.292
well, what would happen was,
the fight would be coming

00:05:26.292 --> 00:05:28.490
it's a week away and I'm
so excited I can't wait,

00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:30.484
I'm watching everything,
I'm reading everything

00:05:30.484 --> 00:05:32.777
that leads up to the fight, right?

00:05:32.777 --> 00:05:34.855
It's the night of the fight,
got all my buddy's over,

00:05:34.855 --> 00:05:36.655
we bought all the pizza and the beer,

00:05:36.655 --> 00:05:38.312
and we're ready to roll,

00:05:38.312 --> 00:05:40.328
and a fight never happens.

00:05:40.328 --> 00:05:43.017
These guys run around for twelve rounds

00:05:43.017 --> 00:05:44.610
and the fight doesn't happen.

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:45.591
Do you know why?

00:05:45.591 --> 00:05:48.353
Do you know why this has
happened and why boxing is dying?

00:05:48.353 --> 00:05:51.494
Because the sport has become so greedy,

00:05:51.494 --> 00:05:54.339
nobody was ever thinking
about the future of the sport.

00:05:54.339 --> 00:05:56.326
It's about how much money
we can all put in our pocket

00:05:56.326 --> 00:05:58.073
right here right now.

00:05:58.073 --> 00:05:59.663
Who cares about tomorrow.

00:05:59.663 --> 00:06:01.527
So essentially what you get at the end,

00:06:01.527 --> 00:06:04.860
is you get two multimillionaires, right?

00:06:06.324 --> 00:06:07.880
Who step into the ring and

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:10.336
do everything they can to avoid a fight

00:06:10.336 --> 00:06:12.118
so they can win, just barely win,

00:06:12.118 --> 00:06:14.772
to get to the next
multimillion dollar fight

00:06:14.772 --> 00:06:16.689
that we pay for, right?

00:06:17.974 --> 00:06:22.033
And it just became ridiculous
and it's exactly what goes...

00:06:22.033 --> 00:06:24.052
Think about this, think about every person

00:06:24.052 --> 00:06:26.038
in this room right now.

00:06:26.038 --> 00:06:29.705
If I guaranteed you all
$37 million dollars,

00:06:30.549 --> 00:06:33.966
guaranteed $37 million dollars this year,

00:06:34.903 --> 00:06:36.806
Guess what you're going to do?

00:06:36.806 --> 00:06:38.389
Not much, not much.

00:06:40.129 --> 00:06:42.497
Are you going to bust your ass every day?

00:06:42.497 --> 00:06:44.098
Your alarm's going to go off
in the morning and you're

00:06:44.098 --> 00:06:46.023
like, I'm not going to go to class.

00:06:46.023 --> 00:06:47.075
What the hell do I want
to go to class for?

00:06:47.075 --> 00:06:48.335
I got $37 million dollars.

00:06:48.335 --> 00:06:49.687
(audience laughs)

00:06:49.687 --> 00:06:50.675
Right?

00:06:50.675 --> 00:06:54.132
Who's going to class if they've
got $37 million dollars?

00:06:54.132 --> 00:06:56.263
Nobody's going to class.

00:06:56.263 --> 00:06:58.055
You know what happens when
you get $37 million dollars

00:06:58.055 --> 00:07:00.030
and you're a fighter?

00:07:00.030 --> 00:07:01.186
(audience laughs)

00:07:01.186 --> 00:07:03.336
I don't want to get punched in the face.

00:07:03.336 --> 00:07:05.332
I got $37 million dollars, man.

00:07:05.332 --> 00:07:06.710
(audience laughs)

00:07:06.710 --> 00:07:08.419
I'm not getting punched in the face.

00:07:08.419 --> 00:07:09.897
This is ridiculous.

00:07:09.897 --> 00:07:12.550
We incentivize guys to fight.

00:07:12.550 --> 00:07:16.642
You get money to show,
and you get money to win.

00:07:16.642 --> 00:07:18.614
And then you get money for
the best fight of the night,

00:07:18.614 --> 00:07:19.729
you get money for the best knockout,

00:07:19.729 --> 00:07:22.008
money for the best submission.

00:07:22.008 --> 00:07:23.045
You're incentivized.

00:07:23.045 --> 00:07:25.913
No different than any other
business in the world.

00:07:25.913 --> 00:07:27.074
Show up at your job

00:07:27.074 --> 00:07:31.178
and have a half-assed
day, see how that goes.

00:07:31.178 --> 00:07:32.993
Nah, I'm not in the mood today.

00:07:32.993 --> 00:07:34.181
See how that goes.

00:07:34.181 --> 00:07:36.233
You have to be incentivized.

00:07:36.233 --> 00:07:40.641
When somebody hires you, when
you guys leave this school

00:07:40.641 --> 00:07:43.223
and go to these other jobs,
you will cut out a deal

00:07:43.223 --> 00:07:45.160
where you're working for some big company

00:07:45.160 --> 00:07:47.875
where you'll have incentives and bonuses.

00:07:47.875 --> 00:07:49.580
It's the way the real world works.

00:07:49.580 --> 00:07:52.169
Boxing does not live in
the real world anymore.

00:07:52.169 --> 00:07:53.700
And that's why it's hurting.

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:58.092
Well the first time that I
really got involved in UFC was,

00:07:58.092 --> 00:08:02.229
everybody had seen UFC
1, you know, I saw UFC 1,

00:08:02.229 --> 00:08:04.164
but when we got involved
and it was because

00:08:04.164 --> 00:08:05.909
we started taking jiu jitsu,

00:08:05.909 --> 00:08:08.405
and through jiu jitsu we
fell in love with this sport,

00:08:08.405 --> 00:08:10.910
and then we started to
meet some of the athletes,

00:08:10.910 --> 00:08:13.125
and when I say we, I mean me
and the Fertitta brothers,

00:08:13.125 --> 00:08:17.685
and it was really, you know,
learning about the sport

00:08:17.685 --> 00:08:19.515
and meeting the athletes that

00:08:19.515 --> 00:08:23.443
completely got us, literally,
addicted to the sport.

00:08:23.443 --> 00:08:26.313
Then when we went to our
first ever UFC event,

00:08:26.313 --> 00:08:31.191
it was down in New Orleans
at the UNO arena down there,

00:08:31.191 --> 00:08:33.673
and literally, me, Frank
and Lorenzo were sitting

00:08:33.673 --> 00:08:35.986
in the audience going holy (bleep),

00:08:35.986 --> 00:08:38.325
imagine if they did this and
imagine if they did that,

00:08:38.325 --> 00:08:40.260
this thing could be big.

00:08:40.260 --> 00:08:43.343
Then, once we bought it, our goal was

00:08:45.076 --> 00:08:49.190
and always has been to
make this a global sport.

00:08:49.190 --> 00:08:51.372
The thing is with the guys like Mike

00:08:51.372 --> 00:08:53.248
is as human beings we're fascinated by

00:08:53.248 --> 00:08:55.190
who the toughest guys in the world are.

00:08:55.190 --> 00:08:56.023
We are.

00:08:56.023 --> 00:08:57.912
You know, I say this all the time,

00:08:57.912 --> 00:09:00.818
if you think of all sports, right?

00:09:00.818 --> 00:09:03.937
And people in here are probably
football fans, baseball,

00:09:03.937 --> 00:09:06.857
basketball, whatever it
is, and take Jordan who's

00:09:06.857 --> 00:09:10.158
probably arguably the most
famous player of all times,

00:09:10.158 --> 00:09:13.869
you know, do people really
know Jordan all over the world

00:09:13.869 --> 00:09:17.184
in every little country
in every...you know.

00:09:17.184 --> 00:09:20.154
You know, Wayne Gretsky,
the list goes on and on.

00:09:20.154 --> 00:09:22.682
It's like, right, I'd
like somebody, anybody,

00:09:22.682 --> 00:09:24.879
and maybe this'll be the
first time it'll ever happen

00:09:24.879 --> 00:09:27.019
if somebody in here tell
me who the greatest cricket

00:09:27.019 --> 00:09:28.188
player on earth is?

00:09:28.188 --> 00:09:30.763
(audience laughs)

00:09:30.763 --> 00:09:32.568
Nobody? Yeah I didn't think so.

00:09:32.568 --> 00:09:34.683
- How great would it be if he was here?

00:09:34.683 --> 00:09:37.887
(audience laughs)

00:09:37.887 --> 00:09:39.694
- Anil just went and killed himself.

00:09:39.694 --> 00:09:41.199
- I've done that a
million times and not one

00:09:41.199 --> 00:09:42.231
person's ever said I know
who the greatest cricket

00:09:42.231 --> 00:09:47.056
player is, but my point
is, anywhere in the world

00:09:47.056 --> 00:09:49.146
everybody knows Mike Tyson,

00:09:49.146 --> 00:09:51.052
everybody knows Muhammad Ali.

00:09:51.052 --> 00:09:52.897
Bruce Lee died in the early 70's,

00:09:52.897 --> 00:09:55.752
does anybody in this room
not know who Bruce Lee is?

00:09:55.752 --> 00:09:58.004
Everybody knows who Bruce
Lee is, he died in the 70's.

00:09:58.004 --> 00:09:59.219
- And it's not like they're promoting him.

00:09:59.219 --> 00:10:01.992
It's not like anybody's promoting him.

00:10:01.992 --> 00:10:03.925
- As human being's we're fascinated by who

00:10:03.925 --> 00:10:05.327
the toughest guy in the world is.

00:10:05.327 --> 00:10:07.029
It's always been that way,

00:10:07.029 --> 00:10:09.766
from the days of the Roman gladiators.

00:10:09.766 --> 00:10:11.086
You know, I always have
this thing where I say

00:10:11.086 --> 00:10:13.446
I can throw all kinds of
stats and bull (bleep)

00:10:13.446 --> 00:10:16.081
you about the UFC that's
true and all these things,

00:10:16.081 --> 00:10:18.708
but here's something that I
don't know if this is true

00:10:18.708 --> 00:10:21.303
but its what I truly believe,
and its what we built

00:10:21.303 --> 00:10:22.703
this company on,

00:10:22.703 --> 00:10:25.603
I believe that before a man
threw a ball through a circle,

00:10:25.603 --> 00:10:28.087
before a man hit a ball with a stick,

00:10:28.087 --> 00:10:30.275
two men were put on this
earth, somebody threw a punch,

00:10:30.275 --> 00:10:32.535
and whoever was standing
around ran over and watched.

00:10:32.535 --> 00:10:34.883
Fighting is the first sport ever

00:10:34.883 --> 00:10:36.297
and it will be the last sport ever.

00:10:36.297 --> 00:10:37.784
It will be around until the day we die.

00:10:37.784 --> 00:10:39.896
Till the earth no longer exists.

00:10:39.896 --> 00:10:41.695
Fighting will always be there.

00:10:41.695 --> 00:10:43.114
If you don't think the UFC is exciting,

00:10:43.114 --> 00:10:44.204
